{"id": "section-body-04101", "title": "Mpox", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Viral Infections", "Mpox"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-04101", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Mpox", "runs": [{"text": "Mpox"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-04102", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Mpox, previously known as monkeypox, is a viral illness caused by the monkeypox virus, a species of the genus Orthopoxvirus. There are two distinct clades of the virus: clade I (with subclades Ia and Ib) and clade II (with subclades IIa and IIb).", "runs": [{"text": "Mpox,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "previously"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "known"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monkeypox,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "illness"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monkeypox"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "species"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "genus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Orthopoxvirus. There are two distinct clades of the virus: clade I (with subclades Ia and Ib) and clade II (with subclades IIa and IIb)."}]}, {"id": "body-04104", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04105", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Mpox causes signs and symptoms which usually begin within a week but can start 1–21days after exposure. Symptoms typically last 2–4 weeks but may last longer in someone with a weakened immune system. They include acute onset of fever (>38.5°C) and chills, headache, sore throat, myalgia (muscle pain/body aches), back pain, profound weakness, or fatigue, acute  skin rash, mucosal lesions or lymphadenopathy (swollen lymph nodes).", "runs": [{"text": "Mpox causes signs and symptoms which usually begin within a week but can start 1–21days after exposure. Symptoms typically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "last"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2–4"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "last"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "longer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "someone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weakened"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immune"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "system."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "They"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "onset"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever (>38.5°C) and chills, headache, sore throat, myalgia (muscle pain/body aches), back pain, profound weakness, or fatigue, acute"}, {"text": "  "}, {"text": "skin rash, mucosal lesions or lymphadenopathy (swollen lymph nodes)."}]}, {"id": "body-04106", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "The skin rash may include single or multiple lesions in the ano-genital region or elsewhere on the body.", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "skin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rash"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "single"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "multiple"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lesions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ano-genital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "region"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "elsewhere"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"